1
00:00:32,608 --> 00:00:35,104
=Love Actually S5=

2
00:00:35,997 --> 00:00:37,600
(Wuzhen, 4:30 AM)

3
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,520
Go.

4
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:39,560
Let's go.

5
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:40,720
Let me grab my phone.

6
00:00:44,608 --> 00:00:45,280
(Watching the sunrise with you)

7
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:45,960
Do you remember

8
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:48,000
the sunrise by the sea we missed?

9
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,160
I've always remembered it,

10
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,680
and I've been looking forward to it.

11
00:00:53,696 --> 00:00:57,280
(A sudden rainstorm coming)

12
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,040
Woke up at 3 AM.

13
00:00:59,040 --> 00:00:59,920
However, it started raining
when we came out.

14
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,000
We're done for, no sunrise.

15
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,600
Let's go wander...

16
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,600
around Wuzhen in the early morning.

17
00:01:11,552 --> 00:01:15,072
(Wuzhen on a rainy day)

18
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:20,240
What's wrong?

19
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:21,600
What's wrong?

20
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:22,440
It's cold.

21
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:23,200
Come nearer.

22
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:26,440
It's pretty cold
over there on your side.

23
00:01:33,856 --> 00:01:34,656
A bit...

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:35,400
It's really cold.

25
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,320
You should wear...

26
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,760
Oh, no, it's thundering.

27
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:49,440
Hurry, let's go.

28
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:51,920
I'm so scared of thunder.

29
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:53,120
Yeah.

30
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,960
What was that? A lightening?

31
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:55,720
I'm really scared.

32
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,000
I'm scared of thunder.

33
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:09,800
It's okay. I'm here.

34
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,520
If lightning strikes,
it'd strike me first.

35
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,000
It wouldn't hit you.

36
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,920
Actually, this feeling is pretty nice.

37
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:22,040
This view is just so beautiful.

38
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,600
It's just a bit cold.

39
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,600
I think good thing we got up early.

40
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:36,920
Even if we couldn't see the sunrise,

41
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,080
this view is very much worth it.

42
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,080
Okay.

43
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:43,800
That's true.

44
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,480
It's really beautiful.

45
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,600
It's also beautiful here.

46
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,520
Isn't my hair too...

47
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,160
It looks too much like a comma.

48
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,200
It looks quite good.

49
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:55,280
Really?

50
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,280
It looks quite good.

51
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:56,960
Come on, then.

52
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:03,880
Beautiful.

53
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,720
These raindrops.

54
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,600
Like pearls large and small
falling on a jade plate.

55
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,480
Right?

56
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Now I love this ancient town even more.

57
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,760
At this moment, get a bowl

58
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,200
of tofu pudding.

59
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,520
Do you want sweet
or savory tofu pudding?

60
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:36,720
Either is fine for me.

61
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,360
Same here.

62
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,560
Well, in this atmosphere,

63
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,560
we should go for savory.

64
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:43,200
I'd like some fried dough sticks.

65
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:43,840
Let's go.

66
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,600
If we head over now,

67
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,360
we'll probably get there

68
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:55,880
around 6:30 AM, or 6:40 AM.

69
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,240
Perfect, the rain is lighter.

70
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,320
(The creative urge strikes again)
Come on.

71
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,040
Okay.

72
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,280
Be careful not to fall.

73
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:25,400
I won't.

74
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,120
It looks quite good.

75
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,160
It stopped raining again.

76
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,600
Where can you take a couple
of solo shots for me?

77
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:39,680
Or...

78
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,440
Or just here, take a few shots for me.

79
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:42,640
Okay.

80
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,280
Yeah.

81
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:45,200
This feeling is wonderful.

82
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,200
My legs look a bit too short.

83
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,440
How come they look short?

84
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,560
This picture is very well-taken.

85
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,200
Look, you should...

86
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:57,640
The two points...
The top area is way too empty.

87
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,400
You need to go down
and angle it up a bit.

88
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,120
Alright.

89
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:00,680
Let me do it.

90
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,200
Trust me.

91
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,480
The bottom frame

92
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,080
should reach about my feet.

93
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:11,840
I know.

94
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,840
Leave less empty space at the bottom.

95
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:20,600
It's not a problem
with my photography skills.

96
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:22,000
Zhou Youling.

97
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,200
What are you laughing at? Look at you.

98
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:29,200
What's so funny?

99
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:31,640
If you're like this,
I'm not happy taking photos.

100
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:32,720
Don't be like that.

101
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,960
I'm laughing at myself.

102
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:34,400
Let me see.

103
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:38,360
You...

104
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:39,760
You...

105
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:40,920
This is a problem with your skill.

106
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:43,120
You think it's not a problem
with your skill?

107
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,240
I told you to make the feet...

108
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,120
There is.

109
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:45,600
Look, isn't this...

110
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,400
You...

111
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:49,880
This one is okay. It's passable.

112
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,760
This one is passable.

113
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:57,680
Fine, maybe you're just too short.

114
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,440
Making that angle is very...

115
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,400
That's not right. If you're too short,

116
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,680
the angle should be right.

117
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:03,000
No, let me try again.

118
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,320
Go back over there.

119
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,440
Let me retake the photo, hurry.

120
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,040
It's a problem with your phone.

121
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:13,960
So when I take photos of you,
isn't it always...

122
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:16,800
Handsome.

123
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:18,960
I always make you look taller
in the photos.

124
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:22,240
This one is not bad.

125
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:23,480
It's a good shot.

126
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:25,960
Just this one.

127
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:27,880
With an umbrella head.

128
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,240
Human head umbrella.

129
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:46,840
People really do laugh
when they're speechless.

130
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:48,960
This is the best shot you've taken.

131
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,480
It makes me look quite slim.

132
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,280
So it's your photography skill issue.

133
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,240
This one you've taken is a good one.

134
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:58,440
- Need to walk along this side.
- I want to eat a lot.

135
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,880
Need to walk along this side.

136
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:02,200
Over there.

137
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,560
It looks like some people
already started eating.

138
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:15,760
Is it good?

139
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,640
Let's have some small wontons.

140
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,320
Do you have small wontons?

141
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:23,880
Yes.

142
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:24,360
One serving, please.

143
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:24,600
Okay.

144
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,360
Here. One bowl
of small wontons is ready.

145
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,280
Okay, thanks.

146
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,120
Please hold it with both hands.

147
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:29,760
Okay.

148
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,360
Let me hold it.

149
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:31,560
I'll hold it. You take this.

150
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,360
You're very dangerous.

151
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,600
If it slips,
the bowl of soup will fly out.

152
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:38,760
Do you want
to have some fried dough sticks?

153
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,280
You want this?

154
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:41,720
One more bite.

155
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:43,840
Give it to me.

156
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:48,880
Delicious, super delicious.

157
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:50,720
I feel like this thin noodle
is my favorite.

158
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,040
You take a bite first.

159
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,120
You give me the first bite.

160
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,400
You eat.

161
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,560
There's no pork lard residue over there.
I didn't mix it well enough.

162
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,440
It's just so delicious!

163
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,360
So tasty.

164
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:08,600
You can try mine.

165
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:13,240
You gave me the meatball in vain.

166
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:13,720
You won't eat it?

167
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,080
I think this bowl of noodles
can be called

168
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:18,880
a delicacy.

169
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:22,760
When I took the first bite,

170
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,680
my eyes lit up.

171
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:32,440
Where are the willow trees?

172
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:37,680
We watched the daybreak.

173
00:08:46,112 --> 00:08:48,704
(Changsha)

174
00:08:48,704 --> 00:08:52,000
(Yang Xihui and Ling Lizheng)

175
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,080
Babe, let me put the glasses
in your bag.

176
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:01,840
Okay.

177
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,160
Don't lean back anymore.

178
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,440
The hair on the back of your head
is flat again.

179
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,720
Hunan is most famous
for its flavored crawfish.

180
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,200
Rice noodles.

181
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,720
Hunan cuisine is also tasty.

182
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:26,400
I'm so hungry.

183
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:27,440
Now that you mention it...

184
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:28,720
We're about to eat soon.

185
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:30,400
I'm starving.

186
00:09:35,784 --> 00:09:37,920
(Hunan Rice Noodle Museum)

187
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:43,320
Let's go.

188
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,480
A big cafeteria.

189
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:47,264
(Hands holding tight)

190
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:49,400
Let me put on my glasses.

191
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,120
I can't see clearly.

192
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,960
Which is the most signature rice noodle?

193
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,040
Would you like Changde rice noodles

194
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,320
or our local ones?

195
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:58,320
Hello.

196
00:09:58,320 --> 00:09:59,200
What did she say?

197
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,440
Round or flat noodles?

198
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,920
(Confused)

199
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,280
Right?

200
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:03,960
Here's the menu.

201
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,080
Can we add extra meat?

202
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,200
Yes, you can add toppings.

203
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:10,800
Double toppings.

204
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:11,920
Add toppings.

205
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,600
What are toppings?

206
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,760
Toppings are the dishes
on top of the noodles.

207
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,160
(Spicy beef rice noodle)
I'd like spicy beef rice noodle.

208
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,960
(Steamed ribs, Steamed pork trotters)
Add steamed ribs, steamed pork trotters,

209
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,400
(Braised pork)
and braised pork.

210
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:24,480
(Young man,
you can eat quite a lot, huh?)

211
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,720
Can we add toppings like that?

212
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:26,640
You can.

213
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:26,960
Okay.

214
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,080
Thank you.

215
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,600
Flat noodles it is.

216
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:29,960
Check, please.

217
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,760
I'm starting to drool.

218
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,400
I'm hungry too.

219
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,200
I'm so hungry.

220
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,120
Let's dig in.

221
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:41,680
Take a photo.

222
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:44,320
This is so lavish.

223
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,000
Make a heart gesture.

224
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:00,840
Come on. Let's eat.

225
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,600
Dig in.

226
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:05,960
Would you like to try

227
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,240
my round noodles?

228
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,200
How can I pick these up?

229
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:12,200
Okay, thank you.

230
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,920
For Hunan people's breakfast,

231
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:27,400
many people just slurp
a bowl of rice noodles.

232
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:29,840
So this is the taste of old Changsha.

233
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:30,560
This is just the flavor.

234
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,200
I think adding three toppings
has made it delicious.

235
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,360
You're sweating bullets.

236
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:38,120
On both sides.

237
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,240
Encounter Token.

238
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,920
What do people usually make?

239
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,360
We have silver jewelry making,

240
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,200
woodworking,

241
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,320
and clay crafting.

242
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:08,560
We'll make rings.

243
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:09,200
Let's make rings.

244
00:12:10,538 --> 00:12:13,568
(Today's date: Customized couple rings)

245
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:16,560
Okay.

246
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:19,600
Well, the first step is

247
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,720
to use this iron ring

248
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,320
to measure the finger
you want to wear it on.

249
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,720
There are numbers on it.

250
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,960
Just tell me your size.

251
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:26,760
Which finger would you pick?

252
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,240
Any finger.

253
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,520
But which finger are you measuring?

254
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,400
I'll take off my ring

255
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:34,320
and try which finger it fits.

256
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:36,440
(Middle finger ring size: 13)
Thirteen.

257
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:39,240
I think size 13 is large enough for me.

258
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,520
I wear size 13. Here you go.

259
00:12:43,456 --> 00:12:44,920
(Ring on the ring finger)

260
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:45,640
Okay, my size is 14.

261
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,440
Yours is 14?

262
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:47,920
Yeah, mine is 14.

263
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:48,630
(The couple's ring sizes)

264
00:12:48,630 --> 00:12:49,440
(Yang Xihui's middle finger size: 13)

265
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,240
(Ling Lizheng's ring finger size: 14)
Such thin fingers.

266
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:51,960
Yeah.

267
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,080
Well, the first step,

268
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,680
take the silver strip.

269
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:55,480
There are thick and thin ones.

270
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:57,480
First engrave your name and the date.

271
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:59,080
You can find them in the box.

272
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:00,400
Engrave that phrase...

273
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:02,200
Hakuna Matata, no worries.

274
00:13:02,528 --> 00:13:03,698
(Customized couple rings,
Yang Xihui, Ling Lizheng)

275
00:13:03,698 --> 00:13:06,200
(Hakuna Matata: No worries,
dreams on track, all good from here)

276
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,000
Okay, ready.

277
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,480
Just tap the hammer once, not too hard.

278
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:10,760
And it'll be engraved.

279
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:11,960
Let me try.

280
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:12,760
Yes.

281
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:13,880
Let me try.

282
00:13:18,608 --> 00:13:19,904
(Gone too hard)

283
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:21,400
